Title: 0011-quiet-debug-prints
Repository: micropoliscore
Base-Commit: 69ccf87ed72d2d2950b70cf16ef1391439bd9d48
Requires: 0010-big-endian-hosts.patch
Author: AmigaOS 3.x port
Date: 2026-11-05
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: generic - any platform

Problem:
  init() prints "init" and destroyMapArrays() prints the map pointer on stdout, which on AmigaOS lands in the Shell the game was started from.
Solution:
  Keep both prints behind MICROPOLIS_DEBUG.
Validation:
  cross-compiled for m68k-amigaos.
Removal:
  Permanent fix.

diff --git a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/allocate.cpp b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/allocate.cpp
index cae10b5..e3e6c7a 100644
--- a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/allocate.cpp
+++ b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/allocate.cpp
@@ -120,7 +120,9 @@ void Micropolis::initMapArrays()
 /** Free all map arrays */
 void Micropolis::destroyMapArrays()
 {
+#ifdef MICROPOLIS_DEBUG
     printf("destroyMapArrays: mapBase: %p\n", mapBase);
+#endif
 
     if (mapBase != NULL) {
         freePtr(mapBase);
